            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0783" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg773"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/12–1345: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Truman to
                        General Marshall
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-15">December 15,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">General Marshall</hi>: On your departure for China I
                    wish to send you this last word of encouragement and appreciation. I believe
                    that the development of a strong, united and democratic China is essential. The
                    alternatives seem to me clearly to be disunity or prolonged civil war, neither
                    of which would be in our interests nor in the interests of international peace.
                    I know that the problems involved are not easy ones but I am confident that you
                    will be able to solve them with complete success.</p>
                <p>You carry with you as you enter upon the task ahead of you my full support and
                    complete confidence.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi> S. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Truman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
